  { text: h(`A registry speaks for many agents. A registry can give each agent its own subdomain and key directory, such as ${c('agent-x.registry.example')}, so each agent keeps an identity of its own and sites can tell them apart [31]. The registry holds or publishes all of those keys, so a breach there hits every agent at once: "a compromised registry could already impersonate every agent in its custody" [8]. FORA's Identity Service is such a registry [8].`) },
];

const ASK_CDN = [
  { title: 'Do you verify Web Bot Auth signatures, and whose?', text: h('Cloudflare verifies bots that registered their key directory with it [12]. AWS WAF labels each signed request verified, invalid, expired or unknown [27]. Akamai, HUMAN and Vercel verify ChatGPT\'s cloud browser, by OpenAI\'s guide [28], and DataDome verifies bots that apply through its form [29].') },
  { title: 'Can our rules treat signed, unsigned and failed requests differently?', text: h('AWS WAF lets a custom rule act on its label [27]. Shopify, for one, gives bots that don\'t sign "the strictest limits" [30].') },
  { title: 'Will our bot rules let FORA buyers through?', text: h('Cloudflare\'s built-in check reads the format used before the working group adopted the draft, and rejects the adopted format FORA uses. On Cloudflare, FORA\'s own edge function does the check [12].') },
];
const ASK_TEAM = [
  { title: 'Which of our pages are for sale?', text: 'Only those need a signature check. Open pages stay open.' },
  { title: 'Where would FORA\'s edge function run?', text: h('It\'s a drop-in on Cloudflare Workers, Fastly Compute and Lambda@Edge [7].') },
];

const FORA_STEPS = [
  { text: h('The identity is the domain. An agent is the host that serves its key directory: "If you control the domain, you control the key." A subdomain is a different party [5].') },
  { text: h('Registration carries no password or API key, because the signature is the credential. The Exchange reads who is registering from the verified signature alone [9].') },
  { text: h('Each signature covers more than the minimum: the method, the full address, a digest of the body and a one-time random value. It lives a few minutes. A request that fails the check is rejected, with "No fallback, no degraded mode" [5].') },
  { text: h('The account belongs to the domain, and a key rotation keeps it [5].') },
  { text: h('The signed link names the buyer\'s key, and FORA\'s edge function on your CDN checks it [7].') },
];

const ENG_SIGN = [
  h("Send <code>Signature-Agent</code> as a dictionary and cover your member: <code>(\"@authority\" \"signature-agent\";key=\"sig1\")</code>. Draft -01 says \"Signers MUST send the dictionary form\" [1]."),
  h("The member's value changed between drafts. In -00 it's an origin, and the verifier looks up the well-known path there. In -01 it's the URL of your key set, and a verifier \"fetches that URL directly\" [1, 4]."),
  h("Cloudflare's verifier accepts the earlier quoted-string form, <code>\"https://signature-agent.test\"</code>. It fails the dictionary form and the <code>key</code> component parameter [12]. Draft -01 lets a verifier accept the string form but doesn't require it [1]."),
  h("Google sends <code>g=\"https://agent.bot.goog\"</code>, a dictionary naming its origin, which is the form of draft -00. OpenAI sends the string <code>\"https://chatgpt.com\"</code> [4, 13, 17]."),
  h("Set <code>tag=\"web-bot-auth\"</code>, <code>created</code> and <code>expires</code>, at most 24 hours apart by the draft's recommendation. Set <code>keyid</code> to the key's base64url JWK SHA-256 thumbprint (RFC 7638; RFC 8037 Appendix A.3 for Ed25519) [1]."),
  h("Cover <code>@authority</code> or <code>@target-uri</code>. A signature over <code>@authority</code> alone \"verifies against any method, path, or body sent to that authority until it expires\" [1]."),
  h("To narrow it, also cover <code>@method</code> and <code>@path</code> or <code>@target-uri</code>, and send and cover <code>Content-Digest</code> for a body. The draft sets no nonce rule. Cloudflare says \"there is currently no nonce validation\" and, of <code>expires</code>, \"A minute is often sufficient\" [1, 12]."),
  h("Algorithms should be registered in the HTTP Message Signatures algorithm registry, and the draft's test vectors use Ed25519 and RSA-PSS with SHA-512. Cloudflare \"accepts all valid Ed25519 keys found in your key directory\" [1, 12]."),
  h("Serve the directory over https as a JWK Set. At the well-known path its media type must be <code>application/http-message-signatures-directory+json</code> [1]."),
  h("Sign the response once per key over <code>\"@authority\";req</code> and <code>content-digest</code>. The draft recommends it, and Cloudflare requires it before it registers a directory [1, 12]."),
  h("Rotate in three steps: add the new key before you use it, keep the old one until it expires, then remove it, so \"the directory's cache lifetime bounds how long a removed key keeps verifying\". The draft \"defines no revocation\" [1]."),
];
const ENG_VERIFY = [
  h("Fetch the member's URL over https, accept only a 200 and follow no redirects. Guard the fetch against server-side request forgery. Attach no policy to the URL until a key from it verifies the signature [1]."),
  h("\"Key lookup MUST be keyed on the (URL, key) pair, not on the key alone\" [1]."),
  h("Cache the directory under normal HTTP caching rules and refresh it when it goes stale. A failed fetch \"MUST NOT evict a cached entry\", and failed lookups should stay cached five minutes at most [1]."),
  h("To ask for a signature, send <code>Accept-Signature</code>, usually with a 403. A signature or nonce used more often than your policy allows can get a 429. Whether to require nonces \"is deployment policy\" [1]."),
];
const ENG_FORA = [
  h("FORA signs the profile of draft -00, the one the working group adopted on September 1, 2026. A -00 verifier checks a FORA signature without knowing FORA, and ignores the members FORA adds to its directory [4, 5]."),
  h("Its <code>Signature-Agent</code> is a dictionary naming the signer's https origin, such as <code>sig1=\"https://research.acme.com\"</code>, covered with the <code>key</code> parameter. Cloudflare's verifier rejects that form [5, 12]."),
  h("On every FORA call the signature also covers <code>@method</code>, <code>@target-uri</code>, <code>content-digest</code> and <code>authorization</code>, sent empty when there's no token. It carries a fresh 64-byte random <code>nonce</code> [5]."),
  h("The lifetime is \"a few minutes\", and the docs' example uses 300 seconds. A FORA verifier that keeps a replay store refuses a signature it has already accepted [5]."),
  h("A FORA directory must be signed. Each key is Ed25519 and carries <code>not_before</code> and <code>not_after</code>. A FORA verifier follows only members of -00's default <code>directory</code> type, so it ignores a <code>jwks_uri</code> or <code>cimd</code> member [5]."),
  h("A directory may name a <code>revocation_url</code>. FORA verifiers poll it every 300 seconds, with 10% jitter, and each list revokes only its own keys [5]."),
  h("In Web Bot Auth the identity is the directory's URL. FORA narrows it to the host, and a subdomain is a different party [5]."),
  h("A signed link names the thumbprint of the buyer's key. The buyer sends its public key with the fetch, so the edge function checks the link, the thumbprint and the signature without fetching the buyer's directory [7]."),
  h("An agent on its own domain holds its own key. On FORA's Identity Service, the service creates the key, \"keeps the private key in its key store\" and signs for the agent [8]."),
  h("The docs name the cost of custody: \"a compromised registry could already impersonate every agent in its custody\" [8]."),
  h("The Identity Service gives \"One developer, one subdomain, one key\". The subdomain is random and \"leaks no identity\", and it's the same at every Exchange, so Exchanges can link one developer's requests across them [1, 8]."),
];

